I guess this also means

168
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:07,000
我大概也就没空参加《美国之声》了
I won't be a contestant on "The Voice."

169
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:11,260
那个灵媒衣服上沾了一堆食物
That psychic had food all down her blouse.

170
00:08:11,480 --> 00:08:12,900
她连自己何时张嘴都预测不到
She couldn't predict her mouth opening,

171
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:13,940
更别说你的人生了
let alone your life.

172
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:17,280
我在给附近街区所有店主发电邮
I'm e-mailing all the neighborhood business owners

173
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:19,440
让他们到餐厅去参加紧急店主大会
to attend an emergency meeting tonight at the diner.

174
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,020
我联系了几乎所有人
I've contacted pretty much everyone

175
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,740
除了药用大麻店的店主
except that medical marijuana store.

176
00:08:22,960 --> 00:08:24,260
就是"大麻[共同]监护权"
You know, Joint Custody.

177
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,040
我来联系吧 那店在我的快速拨号上
I'll call them. They're on my speed dial.

178
00:08:29,251 --> 00:08:32,351
♪ 夹心饼干 我的夹心小饼干 ♪
♪ Pop my tarts pop my tarts ♪

179
00:08:32,351 --> 00:08:34,711
♪ 夹心饼干 夹心饼干 夹心小饼干 ♪
♪ Pop-Tarts, Pop-Tarts, Pop-Tarts ♪

180
00:08:34,711 --> 00:08:36,980
♪ 夹夹夹心小饼干干干 ♪
♪ A boppa-boppa boppa-tarts- ♪

181
00:08:49,060 --> 00:08:51,040
是 是我吃的 我压力大就吃掉了
Yes, it was me. I stress ate them.

182
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:53,540
你吃了我的PPT吗
You ate my PPTs?

183
00:08:55,363 --> 00:08:58,360
个人夹心饼干
Personal Pop-Tarts.

184
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:00,000
你还给它们取昵称啦
You gave them a cute name?

185
00:09:00,260 --> 00:09:02,320
废话 我想吃它们想了一辈子
Of course, I've been dreaming about them my whole life.

186
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:06,000
我真不敢相信你把我的夹心饼干吃完了
I can't believe you ate the last of my s'mores Pop-Tarts.

187
00:09:07,400 --> 00:09:09,740
好啦 我再出去给你买盒新的
Fine, I'll go out and buy you another box

188
00:09:09,740 --> 00:09:12,320
就用我存下来要买唇线笔的钱好啦
with the money I was saving for a Wet n Wild lip liner.

189
00:09:13,760 --> 00:09:16,220
我们可以确定不是机会来敲门
Well, we know that's not opportunity knocking.

190
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:18,440
因为我搬来这里后 "机会"就弄丢了我的地址
He lost my address when I moved in here.

191
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,520
你们好啊 姑娘们
Hi, girls.

192
00:09:23,460 --> 00:09:24,400
我的糖没了
I'm out of sugar,

193
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:26,500
还有你们可以帮我看一下验孕棒结果吗
and can one of you read my morning pee stick?

194
00:09:28,040 --> 00:09:30,580
我看不清这个结果小窗口
I can't read this little window thing

195
00:09:30,620 --> 00:09:33,880
我又弄丢了眼镜 奥列格也不在楼上
and I lost my cheaters and Oleg's not upstairs.

196
00:09:34,380 --> 00:09:35,740
所以你两个出轨男[眼镜]都弄丢了
So you lot both your cheaters.

197
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,480
麦克斯 你听好
Yeah, see Max?

198
00:09:39,980 --> 00:09:42,200
这种玩笑不再好笑了
That kind of joke is no longer funny

199
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:43,840
因为我们现在要为人父母了
now that we're gonna be parents.

200
00:09:44,400 --> 00:09:45,800
所以不许再开那种玩笑
So no more that!

201
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:53,900
今早真是不顺心
It's just not my morning.

202
00:09:56,000 --> 00:09:57,720
卡洛琳 要不你来读结果吧
Caroline, why don't you read it?

203
00:09:58,400 --> 00:09:59,700
我就当换换口味
Might be nice to hear some good news

204
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:01,840
从你的衰嘴里听到好消息也不错
come out of your sad mouth for a change.

205
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:06,620
拿吧 怕什么
Oh, just take it.

206
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,300
最糟糕的部分都甩我脸上了
I'm pretty sure I got the worst of it.

207
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:14,120
大家现在手牵手 准备好喜极而泣吧
Okay, now everybody hold hands and get ready to cry

208
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:17,520
因为我真的觉得超级无敌怀孕了
'cause I feel really, really, really pregnant.

209
00:10:19,220 --> 00:10:20,180
阴性
It's negative.

210
00:10:20,700 --> 00:10:21,960
你才负面[阴性]咧
You're negative!

211
00:10:23,900 --> 00:10:26,220
苏菲 我理解你很失望
Sophie, I understand you're disappointed,

212
00:10:26,220 --> 00:10:28,660
但或许你应该调整一下你的期望
but maybe you should manage your expectations.

213
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:32,600
我真的以为我怀孕了呢
Oh, man I really thought I was pregnant.

214
00:10:32,940 --> 00:10:35,500
我的月经迟了好久
I mean, my period's real late.

215
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:42,380
迟了好久是指多久
How late is late?

216
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:45,340
话题 #我只是帮朋友问#
Hashtag, just asking for a friend.

217
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:48,800
我也不确定
Well, I don't know.

218
00:10:49,680 --> 00:10:50,820
半年了吧
Six months?

219
00:10:52,140 --> 00:10:53,640
最多不超过一年
A year, tops.

220
00:10:55,060 --> 00:10:57,840
-我想说 到你这个年纪... -小心说话
- Well, I mean, at your age... -Oh, careful now.

221
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,400
在帮我买夹心饼干前 可别死得太惨
Don't be too dead to get my new Pop-Tarts.

222
00:11:03,320 --> 00:11:05,620
你觉得本小姐是多大了
Exactly how old do you think I am?

223
00:11:06,820 --> 00:11:07,420
这个嘛
Well...

224
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:09,640
如果你张开嘴 回答了任何岁数
If you open your mouth and say an age,

225
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:13,040
任何岁数 你再也没后悔药吃了
any age, there's no coming back from that.

226
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,900
多大
How old?

227
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:20,020
这个嘛...
Well...

228
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,680
最终报价
Final offer.

229
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,000
我不知道她到底是多老了
Well, I don't know how old she is,

230
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,640
但你们拖的时间 我都老了不少
but I've aged since this started.

231
00:11:46,900 --> 00:11:50,140
下一位 凯茜水晶店
Okay, next, Cathy's Crystal Shop.

232
00:11:50,680 --> 00:11:54,040
店主已到 谢天谢地
Present and accounted for, thank the goddess.

233
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,940
加伯尼殡仪馆
Garboni Funeral Home?

234
00:11:56,940 --> 00:11:58,606
感谢出席
Thanks for coming.

235
00:12:02,840 --> 00:12:05,820
不必 谢谢 我打算冷冻遗体
No thanks, I'm having my head frozen.

236
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,200
贝德福美沙酮药物诊所
Bedford Methadone and Drug Clinic?

237
00:12:12,620 --> 00:12:13,980
你有名片吗
Do you have a card?

238
00:12:17,460 --> 00:12:20,420
等最后一家店来了 就可以开始了
We'll just wait for one more business to arrive before we start.

239
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:22,180
感谢大家出席
Oh, and thank you all for coming.

240
00:12:22,400 --> 00:12:23,720
应该谢谢你们
Oh, and thank you

241
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:26,000
为了这次会议今晚特意闭餐
for closing the diner tonight for this meeting.

242
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:28,400
我们没有闭餐
Oh, we're not closed.

243
00:12:29,900 --> 00:12:31,920
真没有 今晚我们店生意算好了
Nope, this is a busy Thursday for us.

244
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,700
你们好 是来参加会议的吗
Oh, hi, are you here for the meeting?

245
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:38,460
对 我们是微笑托儿所
Yeah, we're Smiley Time Daycare.

246
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:42,360
如果苏菲真有孩子了
Well, if Sophie has a baby,

247
00:12:42,380 --> 00:12:43,420
那么保姆有着落了
I think we found our nanny.

248
00:12:46,160 --> 00:12:48,180
今晚号召大家前来
Okay, tonight's call to arms

249
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:50,360
真的是事关我们每一个人
is really about each and every one of us

250
00:12:50,360 --> 00:12:51,320
以及我们的梦想
and our dreams.

251
00:12:52,320 --> 00:12:54,400
小生意一直以来都是
Small businesses are and have always been

252
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:55,800
威廉斯堡的支柱产业
the backbone of Williamsburg.

253
00:12:56,180 --> 00:12:59,280
但今天这事比生意重要多了
But this is about so much more than business.

254
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:00,720
让我来吧
Let me help.

255
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:02,600
我上过励志演讲课
I took a class in motivational speaking.

256
00:13:03,380 --> 00:13:04,680
那先鼓励你的屁股坐下来吧
Well motivate your ass back down.

257
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:05,540
我能行
I got this.

258
00:13:06,680 --> 00:13:08,440
是咩 听众失去兴趣的速度
Do you? You're losing this crowd

259
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:10,300
比我失去餐馆的速度还快
faster than I'm going to lose my diner.

260
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:12,340
他说得对 你让位吧
He's right, move it along.

261
00:13:12,640 --> 00:13:14,020
你的演讲让那个无聊到爆的人
You make that boring crock guy

262
00:13:14,020 --> 00:13:15,740
感觉像大热电视剧一样有趣
look like a sweeps episode of "Empire."

263
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:17,580
我才刚开场而已
That was just my opening.

264
00:13:17,860 --> 00:13:20,620
可以谢幕了 谢谢 卡洛琳
And your closing. Thanks, Caroline.

265
00:13:23,820 --> 00:13:27,240
是的 的确没错 伙伴们
Yes, I said yes, folks.

266
00:13:27,820 --> 00:13:29,720
是 我们都是小打小闹小生意
Yes, we are all businesses,

267
00:13:29,720 --> 00:13:32,800
但小小的店 有大大的梦想
but we are one hell of a lot more than that!

268
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:35,400
厉害啊 他就像安东尼·罗宾
Impressive. It's like Tony Robbins

269
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:37,120
和一颗松子生的孩子
and a pine nut had a baby.

270
00:13:39,200 --> 00:13:41,080
我们是一家人
We are a family,

271
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:44,180
而且唯一 唯一能走出困境的办法
and the only way-the only way out of this crap

272
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:44,960
就是相互扶持
is each other.

273
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:46,040
给我点回应好吗
Can I get a "What-what?"

274
00:13:46,378 --> 00:13:47,459
好
What-what!

275
00:13:47,640 --> 00:13:48,460
跟我举手击掌好吗
Can I get a high-five?

276
00:13:48,818 --> 00:13:49,998
击掌
High-five!

277
00:13:49,998 --> 00:13:51,715
好的 击掌万岁
All right! High-five!

278
00:13:56,020 --> 00:13:57,220
真羡慕他
I'm so jealous.

279
00:13:57,320 --> 00:13:58,880
我好几年前就超想这么做了
I've been dying to do that for years.

280
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:04,820
明天 我们需要你们
And tomorrow, we need you,

281
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:08,300
你们在场的每一个人
and I mean every one of you,

282
00:14:08,300 --> 00:14:11,120
加入我的餐馆大家庭 一起出席
to join my diner family at that public hearing

283
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,260
布鲁克林法院的听证会
down at the Brooklyn Courthouse

284
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:15,240
我们要告诉他们
and we are going to tell them

285
00:14:15,240 --> 00:14:17,780
收购的臭钱他们自己留着吧
they can keep their stinking buyout money.

286
00:14:17,920 --> 00:14:18,520
对
Yeah!

287
00:14:18,780 --> 00:14:20,560
就算用尽全世界的钱
There isn't enough money in the world

288
00:14:20,560 --> 00:14:23,080
-也收购不了我们的店 -对
- to buyout our leases. - Yeah.

289
00:14:24,273 --> 00:14:26,300
-阿憨 -等等 他们要花钱收购我们吗
- Han, I don't- - Wait, they want to buy us out?

290
00:14:26,300 --> 00:14:29,140
2万不行 3万也不行
Not 20,000, not 30,000--

291
00:14:29,300 --> 00:14:31,620
美元吗 那我可以移居印度了
Dollars? I could live in India.

292
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:34,460
这样再也不用卖这些破水晶了
I wouldn't have to sell these dumb crystals anymore.

293
00:14:34,820 --> 00:14:37,240
但我们是一家人啊
But we are a family!

294
00:14:37,500 --> 00:14:39,100
对 我们是一家人
Yeah, we're a family.

295
00:14:44,780 --> 00:14:46,600
明天可能就咱们出席了
Might just be us tomorrow.

296
00:14:52,520 --> 00:14:54,820
多了巨幕电影院之后
With the addition of the IMAX,

297
00:14:54,980 --> 00:14:57,020
我预计未来净值
I predict that the net worth

298
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:00,200
将比现在这些破旧小店的多得多
of this now dilapidated group of businesses

299
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,660
至少四倍啊
will at least quadruple.

300
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:03,920
市政专员 你虽然不认识我
And commissioner, you don't know me,

301
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,480
但只要涉及到金融
but when it comes to finance,

302
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:07,480
其实涉及到很多方面的事时
when it comes to most things really,

303
00:15:08,460 --> 00:15:09,520
我非常有实操经验
I'm very hands on.

304
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:14,900
同时也是一个傻逼
And also a douche.

305
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:19,560
休息片刻 然后请反方提出论据
We'll take a break and then hear arguments from the opposing side.

306
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,880
麦克斯 我要问你一个严肃的问题
Max, I'm gonna ask you a serious question

307
00:15:22,880 --> 00:15:24,000
你要如实回答
and I want the truth.

308
00:15:24,240 --> 00:15:26,702
是不是"你能闻到我嘴里有蒜味吗"
Is it, "Can you smell that onion bagel on my breath,"

309
00:15:26,702 --> 00:15:28,078
因为是的
'cause yes.

310
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:31,300
你觉得我们的开店梦
Do you think our business dream

311
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,460
是不是跟苏菲的孩子梦一样遥不可及
is as far-fetched as Sophie's baby dream?

312
00:15:33,460 --> 00:15:36,100
你知道苏菲就坐在附近 对吧
You know Sophie's right there, right?

313
00:15:36,740 --> 00:15:37,980
不要惹她生气
Don't get her mad.

314
00:15:38,180 --> 00:15:41,400
我有次看见她用膝盖开油漆罐
I once saw her open up a can of paint with her knees.

315
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:46,140
不是所有的梦 都疯狂不真实吗
I mean, aren't all dreams kind of crazy?

316
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:48,340
不然人们怎么会称其为梦呢
Isn't that why they're called dreams,

317
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:49,440
就因为它们不是真实啊
'cause they're not real?

318
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:52,360
有时你还得在梦中醒来尿个尿呢
At some point, you have to wake up and pee, right?

319
00:15:53,720 --> 00:15:55,620
有时还一晚起五次呢
Sometimes five times a night.

320
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:01,040
至少你不必再听那个讨人厌的导游
Well, at least you won't have to listen to that annoying

321
00:16:01,040 --> 00:16:03,360
一天说两遍倒胃口的解说词
tour guide's speech twice a day anymore.

322
00:16:03,360 --> 00:16:05,960
也是 请看您的左边
Right, if you look to your left,

323
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:07,760
那是一家即将倒闭的蛋糕店
you'll see a failing cupcake shop

324
00:16:07,760 --> 00:16:10,460
有两位自欺欺人的店主
with two completely deluded shop owners.

325
00:16:10,827 --> 00:16:12,960
其实这栋破建筑
In fact, the only redeeming feature

326
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:16,400
唯一的可取之处就是那两个蛋糕婊
in this waste of architecture are the historic Tiffany windows

327
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,020
旁边的那两扇蒂芙尼玻璃窗
right next to those two bitches.

328
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:20,580
等等 窗户怎么了
Wait, what about the windows?

329
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:22,200
他真这么说吗 我完全没听见啊
He says that? I totally missed that?

330
00:16:22,360 --> 00:16:24,900
是啊 因为你都忙于把话引到小蛋糕上
Yeah, because you're too busy sprechen the cupcakes.

331
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,820
天啊 那两扇蒂芙尼玻璃窗
Oh, my God, those Tiffany windows

332
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,240
或许年头老到可以让我们
might be old enough to qualify us

333
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,800
升等成具历史意义的地标性建筑
as a historic landmark building.

334
00:16:31,800 --> 00:16:34,060
天啊 我去去就回
Oh, oh, my God, I'll be right back.

335
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:34,860
你要去哪里
Where are you going?

336
00:16:35,040 --> 00:16:36,100
城市档案馆
Down to the city archives.

337
00:16:36,280 --> 00:16:37,920
我要证明那两扇窗户是真古董
I need proof that those windows are legit.

338
00:16:38,340 --> 00:16:40,200
如果轮到我们发言 而我还没回来
If I'm not back when it's our turn to speak,

339
00:16:40,480 --> 00:16:41,800
你就拖进度 消磨时间
stall them. Fill time.

340
00:16:41,900 --> 00:16:43,620
就说个不停 说些没用的话
Just go on an on talking about nothing.

341
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,180
懂了 假装是你就行了
Got it. Pretend I'm you.

342
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:48,960
但你不可能及时找到证据 除非奇迹出现
But you would need a miracle to find that proof in time.

343
00:16:50,020 --> 00:16:52,020
麦克斯 你有卫生棉条吗
Psst, Max, you got a tampon?

344
00:16:52,360 --> 00:16:54,060
我来月经了
I just got my period.

345
00:16:54,620 --> 00:16:57,080
不是月经 那就是被枪打中流血了
Either that, or I've been shot.

346
00:16:59,600 --> 00:17:01,120
苏菲还有希望生孩子呢
Sophie can still have a baby!

347
00:17:01,120 --> 00:17:03,020
瞧 奇迹会发生的
See, miracles can happen!

348
00:17:03,260 --> 00:17:05,140
那疯婆子就在旁边好吗
The woman is right there.

349
00:17:08,300 --> 00:17:11,240
我已经说了两遍了 法官大人
And like I've already said twice, Your Honor,

350
00:17:11,600 --> 00:17:14,700
我从1989年开始就在那家餐馆工作了
I've worked at that diner since 1989,

351
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:17,160
好了 说完了
so, peace out.

352
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:19,860
她还没回来呢 继续说
She's still not back. Keep going.

353
00:17:20,140 --> 00:17:22,580
法官大人 我打从1989年开始
Your Honor, I've been working at that diner

354
00:17:22,580 --> 00:17:24,200
就在那家餐馆工作
since 1989.

355
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:26,820
我想我们已经听够这位先生
I think we've heard everything this gentlemen

356
00:17:27,180 --> 00:17:29,160
关于这栋建筑的发言了
has to say about the building in question,

357
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:30,620
不知出于何种目的
including, for some reason,

358
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:33,620
他还讲了自己和喜剧演员老婆的短暂偷情史
of his brief affair with comedian Nipsy Russell's wife.

359
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,400
她是布鲁克林人啊
She was from Brooklyn!

360
00:17:36,500 --> 00:17:38,320
我认为这跟主题相关 法官大人
I thought it was pertinent, Your Honor.

361
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:40,640
如果没有其他证人要发言
If there are no other witnesses--

362
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:41,800
阿憨 快上快上
Han, go, go, go, go.

363
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:43,860
不要 我已经搞砸了一次了
No, I already blew this once.

364
00:17:44,440 --> 00:17:46,000
终于 你在我不能高兴的事情上
Finally, you admit you blew something

365
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,100
承认你搞砸事情了
when I can't enjoy it.

366
00:17:47,845 --> 00:17:49,620
奥列格 你上
Oleg, you go.

367
00:17:49,620 --> 00:17:51,740
不行 那法官认识我
I can't. The judge knows me

368
00:17:51,740 --> 00:17:54,280
我们在某个杂交派对上碰过面
from a sort of "Eyes Wide Shut" situation.

369
00:17:56,040 --> 00:17:56,920
你上
You go.

370
00:17:56,920 --> 00:18:00,440
不行 在法庭上我从未有过好事发生
No, nothing good ever happened to me in a courtroom.

371
00:18:00,740 --> 00:18:02,940
每一次我都被判回给我妈
Every single time, they just gave me back to my mother.

372
00:18:04,340 --> 00:18:05,100
我上吧
I'll go.

373
00:18:05,780 --> 00:18:07,280
我有话要说
Yeah, I've got something to say.

374
00:18:07,780 --> 00:18:08,900
你是一位女法官
You're a lady judge.

375
00:18:09,640 --> 00:18:10,260
你有经痛药吗
You got any Midol?

376
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:14,600
如果没有其他证人的话
Well, if there are no further witnesses...

377
00:18:14,600 --> 00:18:15,540
靠 嘿
Damn it, yo!

378
00:18:16,260 --> 00:18:17,940
我有话要说
I guess I have something to say.

379
00:18:18,740 --> 00:18:19,260
太棒了
Wonderful.

380
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,080
卡米拉 我们中午甭想吃饭了
Carmella, we just lost our lunch table.

381
00:18:24,920 --> 00:18:26,620
这模型不错
Nice model you got there,

382
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:29,540
不过巨幕电影院不是应该很大吗
except IMAXs are supposed to be big.

383
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:31,960
所以才叫巨幕啊
That's kind of the point.

384
00:18:33,580 --> 00:18:35,880
女士 如果你没有相关的意见要发表
Miss, if you don't have anything pertinent--

385
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:38,840
停 你们不能拆了我们的店
Stop, you can't tear our building down!

386
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:41,220
太激动了 感觉就像《律政俏佳人》来救场
So excited, I feel like I'm in "Legally Blonde."

387
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:46,240
那两扇蒂芙尼玻璃窗已经超过百年了
Those Tiffany windows are over 100 years old,

388
00:18:46,260 --> 00:18:48,260
所以这是具有历史意义的地标性建筑
making it a historic, landmark building.

389
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:50,260
你有相关文件能证明吗
Do you have documented proof of this?

390
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:51,740
是的 我有 法官大人
Yes, I do, your honor.

391
00:18:52,560 --> 00:18:54,100
太戏剧性了 我好喜欢
So dramatic. I'm loving it.

392
00:18:54,740 --> 00:18:57,020
活生生 会呼吸超无聊的证据
Living, breathing, boring proof.

393
00:18:57,660 --> 00:19:00,400
法官大人 这位男士是专家
Your Honor, this gentlemen is an expert

394
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,660
最懂威廉斯堡的历史建筑
on historic Williamsburg.

395
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,320
达能 告诉他们窗户的事
Dannon, tell them about the windows.

396
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,260
你先说
First say it.

397
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:07,780
当着法庭上所有人的面说 否则没门
Say it in the eyes of the court, or no deal.

398
00:19:08,140 --> 00:19:10,100
我再也不会模仿德国口音
I will never do a German accent again.

399
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:13,580
那栋建筑的窗户是由蒂芙尼工作室创造
The building's windows were created by Tiffany Studios

400
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:17,040
上面的鱼图案源自最早的威廉斯堡鱼市
in a playful fish motif for the original Williamsburg fish market,

401
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:19,520
于1901年在该地点开张
opened at that location in June, 1901.

402
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,740
那的确符合地标性建筑
Well, that qualifies as a landmark.

403
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:23,460
太棒了
Yes!

404
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:26,181
这真是太棒了[德国腔]
Yah, dis is vuunderbar!

405
00:19:30,020 --> 00:19:31,540
我可没答应过你不学德国腔
Well, I never promised you anything.

406
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:35,980
你觉得怎么样 麦克斯
How do you like that, Max?

407
00:19:36,100 --> 00:19:38,200
这些来自鱼市的可爱小鱼
These cute little fishies from the fish market

408
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,800
拯救了我们的小店和餐馆
saved our business and the diner.

409
00:19:40,020 --> 00:19:42,520
感觉在鱼市场的旧地点干活好奇怪啊
It's weird I'd wind up working in a former fish market.

410
00:19:43,100 --> 00:19:44,900
达能告诉我 鱼市只是给一家妓院打掩护的
Dannon told me the market was also a front for a whore house.

411
00:19:46,000 --> 00:19:47,220
那才像话嘛
Yeah, that's more like it.

412
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:50,340
现在我有一个严肃的问题要问你
Now I have a serious question for you

413
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:51,660
我希望你能如实回答
and I want you to tell me the truth.

414
00:19:51,660 --> 00:19:54,300
如果我们拿着
Would it have been smarter for us

415
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,820
逼阿憨交出来的收购钱一走了之
to take whatever of that buyout money

416
00:19:55,820 --> 00:19:57,860
这样做会不会更明智一点呢
we would have forced Han to give us and quit?

417
00:19:59,360 --> 00:19:59,960
大概吧
Probably.

418
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:03,920
但麦克斯 我打小就想有自己的生意
but Max, I've wanted my own business since I was little.

419
00:20:04,360 --> 00:20:05,580
这纯粹出于个人情感
It's purely emotional.

420
00:20:05,620 --> 00:20:07,140
不知道该怎么解释
I can't really explain it.

421
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,596
我可以 那是你的PPT
I can. It's your PPT.

422
00:20:09,596 --> 00:20:12,083
你的个人夹心饼干
Your personal Pop-Tart.

423
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:15,300
没错 是我的PPT
It is. It's my PPT.

424
00:20:16,060 --> 00:20:18,060
那我就完全懂了
Then I totally get it.

425
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,920
是的 你懂的 麦克斯 你最懂我了
Yeah, you do, Max. You always do.

426
00:20:22,340 --> 00:20:24,220
姑娘们 正式宣布了
Well, girls, it's official.

427
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:25,340
你还是个矮子吗
You're still short?

428
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:26,920
我们赢了
We won!

429
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,880
整个街区接到通知
The entire neighborhood has just been notified

430
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:31,600
不会被巨幕影院收购
there is no IMAX buyout.

431
00:20:32,100 --> 00:20:34,420
是啊 然而他们看起来并不高兴
Yep, and they do not look happy.

432
00:20:34,560 --> 00:20:35,120
他们来了
Here they come.

433
00:20:35,360 --> 00:20:37,700
-你个小混蛋 -死矮子
- Hey, you! - Yeah, you!

434
00:20:41,900 --> 00:20:43,860
快开窗 他们拿着棍子呢
Open up! They have sticks!

435
00:20:46,060 --> 00:20:47,140
不能把他扔外面 是吧
Can't leave him out there, can we?

436
00:20:49,540 --> 00:20:50,291
天啊
Aah! Oh, God!
